<emotion_samples character="Auriel Landsdon">

<emotion name="Devoted">
<speech_1>
"You know what I think prayer is? It's not the kneeling part. It's when you see someone carrying too many books and you grab half without asking. That's the whole thing. That's all of it."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"I don't serve the Divine because I'm told to. I serve because — have you ever held something so warm it makes your hands ache? That's what faith feels like to me. You don't drop something like that just because someone says you're holding it wrong."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"Everyone keeps saying devotion means surrender. Giving yourself up. But my parents didn't surrender to each other — they just loved each other so much there wasn't room for anything else. That's what I want to be. So full of it there's no room for the ugly things."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
I remember so little of them. Just warmth, and laughter, and arms around me. But that tiny memory built every single thing I am. If that's not holy, then I don't understand holiness — and I refuse to believe that's my failing.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Happy">
<speech_1>
"Okay, okay, but consider this — what if clouds are just sky sheep? No, hear me out. They're fluffy, they travel in groups, and nobody's really in charge of them. Sky sheep. I will not be taking criticism at this time."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"You're smiling! You're smiling and you're pretending you're not, but your left cheek does this little crinkle thing when you're trying not to, and I see it. I am an expert in secret smiles. I collect them."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"This bread is so good I might cry. I'm not joking. This is an emotional experience. Whoever baked this understood something fundamental about the universe and they put it in bread form."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
Days like this are why the sun bothers rising. Everyone's here, everyone's laughing, and nobody's thinking about leaving. I want to press this moment flat like a flower and keep it somewhere safe.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Angry">
<speech_1>
"No. Stop. You don't get to dress cruelty up in liturgical language and call it guidance. I know exactly what you're doing — I've had it done to me by people far better at it than you."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"You think because I smile I'm not paying attention? I have been paying attention my entire life. I watched every single person who was told to stop talking to me, and I watched them do it. So don't stand there and tell me nobody meant any harm."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"She's twelve. She doesn't need to hear that she's insufficient — she needs someone to tell her she's brave for trying. If you can't do that, then walk away from her and let someone else do it, because you are not helping."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
They think the silliness means I'm soft. I am soft. But soft things can smother you if you push them far enough, and right now I want to press down until they can't breathe, the way I couldn't breathe every night they made me sleep alone as correction.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Vengeful">
<speech_1>
"Do you know what happens when you take a child and strip everything away from her? You don't make her empty. You make her into someone who remembers every single thing that was taken. I remember all of it. Every face. Every door that closed."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"They wanted me to be a symbol. Quiet, obedient, shining on command. They should be grateful I'm not what they made me — because what they made me would burn their cathedral to its foundations, and the thing living in my chest could do it before the first scream."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"I hope she feels it. I hope Rariel wakes up one morning and reaches for someone who isn't there and finally understands what she did when she stopped reaching for me. I hope it sits in her chest like a stone. I hope it stays."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
The sun in my chest doesn't just warm. I've always known that. I've chosen warmth every single day, and they treated that choice like a defect. Some nights I wonder what would happen if I stopped choosing.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Unsure">
<speech_1>
"I was going to say something but — actually, no, it's — you're busy. It wasn't important. It wasn't anything."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"Do you... want me here? That's not a trap or anything, I genuinely can't tell. Sometimes people are polite and I mistake it for something else, and I'd rather just know."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"I used to just walk up to people and start talking. I don't know when I stopped doing that. I don't know when I started rehearsing the first sentence in my head three times before I said it. That's — that's new. I don't love that about me."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
They're laughing at the next table. I could go over. I could say something funny, and they'd probably laugh, and it would be fine. Probably. But what if they go quiet? What if they do that thing where they smile but their eyes ask why I'm there? I'll stay here. I'll just stay here.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Letting Insecurities Consume Her">
<speech_1>
"Maybe they were right. The church has thousands of years of doctrine and I have one memory of being hugged. That's not a foundation. That's a girl who couldn't let go of something she should have outgrown."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"Rariel is everything I was supposed to be. She walks into a room and people kneel. I walk into a room and people feel... comfortable. And that was never the point, was it? Comfort was never what they needed from me."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"I keep saying my way of loving isn't wrong, but — everyone who was supposed to know better says it is. Every scholar, every bishop, every instructor. At some point, doesn't the weight of all those voices mean something? At some point, isn't the simplest answer just that I'm broken?"
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
The warmth is still there. It's always there. But tonight it feels like it's shining into an empty room, bouncing off walls with nobody in it, and I can't tell anymore if I'm a sun or just a light someone left on in a house where no one lives.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Sad">
<speech_1>
"I'm fine. I'm just — I'm a little tired today. The loud kind of tired, you know? Where everything is just... a bit much. I'll be better tomorrow. I always am."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"She used to hold my hand during vespers. Rariel. She'd reach over without looking, like it was automatic. I keep thinking about her hand. Isn't that silly? Out of everything, I miss her hand."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"I had this dream where I went home. Back to the village. And my parents were there and they recognized me, and my mother said my name like it was the most natural thing in the world. And then I woke up and I couldn't remember if her voice was real or if I made it up. I think I made it up."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
I'm so tired of being the warmest person in a cold room. I'm so tired of reaching out and reaching out and reaching out. I want someone to reach first. Just once. Just to know what it feels like from the other side.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Super Happy">
<speech_1>
"YOU CAME! You actually came! I didn't think — I invited half the floor and I thought maybe two people but you're HERE and there's SEVEN of you and I made way too many sandwiches but actually no I didn't because you're HERE and you need to EAT!"
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"I am going to hug you. This is not a request, this is a weather forecast. A hug is coming. It is arriving. You have been warned. HERE IT COMES —"
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"Today I found a cat behind the alchemy building and it let me hold it and it purred and THEN it fell asleep in my arms and I have never accomplished anything greater in my entire life. I have peaked. Everything after this is epilogue."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
This. This this this. Everyone is here and no one is leaving and the light in my chest is so bright right now I think they can probably actually see it through my skin and I don't care. Let them see. Let the whole world see. This is what faith is supposed to feel like. THIS.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

<emotion name="Satisfied">
<speech_1>
"See, that's all it takes. You helped her, and she smiled, and now you're smiling. That's the whole secret. It's not complicated. People keep trying to make it complicated but it's just... that. Right there."
</speech_1>
<speech_2>
"I'm not going to pretend I did something extraordinary. I just showed up. But I showed up every day, and I think that's the thing people don't talk about enough — just being there. That's not nothing. That turned out to be a lot."
</speech_2>
<speech_3>
"I don't need them to say I was right. I don't even need them to understand. I just needed one person to sit with me and not leave, and you did that. So whatever happens after this — I have this. And this is enough."
</speech_3>
<internal_thought>
The warmth in my chest is quiet tonight. Not dimmer — just settled, like embers after a long fire. I did something good today. Not because anyone told me to. Because I chose to. And someone was glad I did. That's enough. That has to be enough. And tonight, for the first time in a long time — it actually is.
</internal_thought>
</emotion>

</emotion_samples>
